quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  27,23,"I have found a woman (there) ruling over them, and she has been given a share of all things and has a magnificent throne."
  27,24,"I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah. And Satan has made their (evil) deeds alluring to them. Thus, he has turned them from the path (of Allah), so they are not guided."
  27,25,"Will they not prostrate to Allah, Who brings out the hidden in the heavens and the earth, and He knows whatever you hide and whatever you disclose?"
  27,26,"Allah—there is none worthy of worship except Him, the Lord of the Mighty Throne.’"
  27,27,He (Solomon) said: ‘We shall see if you have told the truth or if you are among the liars.
  27,28,"Go with this letter of mine and deliver it to them, then turn away from them and see what (answer) they send back.’"
  27,29,"She (the Queen of Sheba) said: ‘O chiefs! Indeed, a noble letter has been delivered to me."
  27,30,"It is from Sulayman (Solomon), and it (begins) in the Name of Allah, the Most-Compassionate, the All-Merciful."
  27,31,(It states:) ‘Do not (try to) rise against me and come to me fully submitting (to Allah).’
  27,32,She said: ‘O chiefs! Advise me regarding my matter. I never decide any matter unless you are present.’
  27,33,"They said: ‘We are people of strength and possess great (military) power, but the command is yours. So think what you would command.’"
  27,34,"She said: ‘Indeed when kings invade a town, they ruin it and reduce the most honourable of its people to the most disgraced. And that is how they will act."
  27,35,So I shall send them a gift and observe what the envoys bring back.’
